{
  "requirement": "`AgentConfig` and its backend-specific configuration types implement Serde\nserialization and deserialization. An application can embed them in its own\nconfiguration types; serializing and deserializing a supported configuration\npreserves its settings.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.agent_config.serialization`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. `AgentConfig` and its backend-specific types (`BedrockConfig`, `BedrockCredentials`, `OpenAiConfig`, `OllamaConfig`, plus `OptionValue` and `SecretString`) implement Serde serialization and deserialization.\n2. They can be embedded in an application's own configuration types.\n3. Serializing and then deserializing a supported configuration preserves its settings.\n\n**Coverage**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#mod[tests]/fn[all_backends_preserve_nested_settings_and_credentials]` covers the round-trip obligation for all three backends. For each backend it does the following:\n  - It deserializes a JSON value into `AgentConfig`.\n  - It re-serializes that config and asserts the result equals the original value. This checks the wire form and that no settings are lost.\n  - It then round-trips through a JSON string and asserts the config equals its copy.\n- Settings covered by that test:\n  - The Bedrock case includes `aws_profile`, `region`, and the full credentials with `session_token`.\n  - The Bedrock options include an integer, a nested object, a boolean, and an array that mixes a string, an integer, and a float.\n  - The OpenAI case includes `endpoint`, `api_key`, and nested options.\n  - The Ollama case includes `api_key_env` and a float option.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configuration_debug_hides_credentials]` covers more of the same obligation:\n  - `SecretString` serializes to its plain value and deserializes back equal.\n  - `AgentConfig` rejects an unknown setting.\n- The tests need nothing more to show embedding. The implementation uses plain `#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]` on the config types, and the tests exercise those same derived impls.\n- The backend-specific structs are exercised both as `AgentConfig` variants and directly. `fn[backend_builders_set_only_the_requested_fields]` serializes each of them directly and deserializes `BedrockCredentials`. That test isn't marked for this requirement, but it adds coverage.\n\n**Minor observations, not gaps**\n- The Ollama round-trip case uses `api_key_env` and not `api_key`. That field is a derived `Option<SecretString>` with the same serde attributes as the OpenAI field, which the test does cover. No distinct required behavior is left untested.\n- Optional-field omission and minimal configs are covered elsewhere, for example by the minimal OpenAI deserialization in `fn[openai_inference_options_only_fill_missing_defaults]`.",
